<title>UK: Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall sharply in week.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe Brent liftings fall sharply in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent crude from Britain's Sullom Voe terminal fell to 471,605 tonnes in the week to October 29, down from 947,123 tonnes the previous week, the Shetland Islands Council Marine Operations Department said.</p>
<p>Four cargoes were destined for British refineries. One cargo went to France and another to the U.S.</p>
